{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4896631","formula":"C₁₁H₁₇NO₃","hill":"C11H17NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"2,3,4-trimethoxyphenethylamine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Isomescaline (IM), also known as 2,3,4-trimethoxyphenethylamine (2,3,4-TMPEA) or as TMPEA-3 or 2C-TMA-3, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine and scaline families related to the psychedelic drug mescaline (3,4,5-trimethoxyphenethylamine; 2,3,4-TMPEA). It is one of several possible positional isomers of trimethoxyphenethylamine (TMPEA). In addition, it is the positional isomer of mescaline in which the methoxy groups on the phenyl ring are located at the 2, 3, and 4 positions instead of at the 3, 4, and 5 positions."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":414332,"mass":211.26,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C(=C(C=C1)CCN)OC)OC","inchikey":"PVLFQRLVSMMSQK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2,3,4-trimethoxyphenyl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"414332","atoms":32,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.033,"y":1.78,"z":0.142,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.712,"y":1.787,"z":-0.11,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.11,"y":-0.602,"z":-0.047,"el":"O"},{"x":4.67,"y":-0.801,"z":-0.725,"el":"N"},{"x":1.025,"y":-0.604,"z":0.33,"el":"C"},{"x":2.512,"y":-0.63,"z":0.467,"el":"C"},{"x":0.344,"y":0.603,"z":0.171,"el":"C"},{"x":3.221,"y":-0.753,"z":-0.887,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.045,"y":0.608,"z":0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":0.317,"y":-1.806,"z":0.362,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.753,"y":-0.593,"z":0.075,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.072,"y":-1.8,"z":0.234,"el":"C"},{"x":1.241,"y":2.437,"z":1.39,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.916,"y":2.247,"z":-1.444,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.757,"y":-1.872,"z":-0.004,"el":"C"},{"x":2.876,"y":0.254,"z":1.001,"el":"H"},{"x":2.797,"y":-1.477,"z":1.107,"el":"H"},{"x":2.965,"y":0.096,"z":-1.531,"el":"H"},{"x":2.8